GC_LobbyGameMode : "{A79C4E0A43DEB821}Prefabs/MP/Modes/GC_LobbyGameMode.et" {
 ID "3FBA244EC7091806"
 components {
  GC_LobbyManager "{6A137A39106A4973}" {
   m_aBriefings {
    GC_Briefing "{B3918C7B48258AC2}" {
     m_iOrder 0
     m_sTitle "Summary"
     m_sContent "A British platoon must defend CIMIC House against a large-scale Iraqi assault aimed at overrunning and capturing the compound."\
     ""\
     "Can the garrison hold long enough to force the attackers to withdraw?"\
     ""\
     "<h2>Summary Notes</h2>"\
     "• E-tool usage is strictly forbidden."\
     "• Iraqi forces only to be slotted if missions is <b>FULL</b> or if blufor accept the challenge."\
     "• The mission is <b>LIVE</b> from the moment you enter the game."
     m_eAudience 1
    }
    GC_Briefing "{2CB95E218155FE62}" {
     m_iOrder 1
     m_sTitle "Situation"
     m_sContent "<h2>PRELIMS</h2>"\
     "DTL: 15/08/1990, 1200hr, Al-Hadra, Kuwait."\
     "Weather: Clear, visability 1km+, no forecast of change."\
     ""\
     "<h2>LORE</h2>  "\
     "Following the coalition invasion of Kuwait, Iraqi forces have begun a fighting withdrawal while attempting to delay the coalition advance and retain control of key urban areas. Although the front line continues to move rapidly, isolated pockets of resistance remain determined to hold strategically important positions."\
     ""\
     "Al-Hadra has become one such battleground. British forces have established a fortified compound within the city to coordinate operations and maintain control of the surrounding area. Its location allows coalition forces to observe enemy movement, secure key routes, and project influence across the city."\
     ""\
     "Known locally as CIMIC House, the compound has become a significant obstacle to Iraqi operations. As long as it remains in British hands, Iraqi forces are unable to move freely through Al-Hadra or fully secure the area."\
     ""\
     "With coalition forces continuing their advance elsewhere, Iraqi commanders have committed a large force to seize the compound before it can be reinforced. The garrison now faces a determined assault and must hold its position until the attack is broken."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "UK"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{BE30622D54084DFA}" {
     m_iOrder 2
     m_sTitle "Situation"
     m_sContent "<h2>PRELIMS</h2>"\
     "DTL: 15/08/1990, 1200hr, Al-Hadra, Kuwait."\
     "Weather: Clear, visability 1km+, no forecast of change."\
     ""\
     "<h2>LORE</h2>  "\
     "Following the coalition invasion of Kuwait, Iraqi forces have begun a fighting withdrawal while attempting to delay the coalition advance and retain control of key urban areas. Although the front line continues to move rapidly, isolated pockets of resistance remain determined to hold strategically important positions."\
     ""\
     "Al-Hadra has become one such battleground. British forces have established a fortified compound within the city to coordinate operations and maintain control of the surrounding area. Its location allows coalition forces to observe enemy movement, secure key routes, and project influence across the city."\
     ""\
     "Known locally as CIMIC House, the compound has become a significant obstacle to Iraqi operations. As long as it remains in British hands, Iraqi forces are unable to move freely through Al-Hadra or fully secure the area."\
     ""\
     "With coalition forces continuing their advance elsewhere, Iraqi commanders have committed a large force to seize the compound before it can be reinforced. The garrison now faces a determined assault and must hold its position until the attack is broken."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_IRAQ"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{F09F0E6744E793B6}" {
     m_iOrder 3
     m_sTitle "Enemy forces"
     m_sContent "<h2>COMPOSITION & DISPOSITION</h2>  "\
     "Enemy forces consist of approximately 300 Iraqi Army personnel from a battalion known as the \"Mahdi Army\", operating throughout the area."\
     ""\
     "<h2>STRENGTHS & CAPABILITIES</h2>  "\
     "• Low quantities of limited armoured support, including BTRs, BRDMs, and BMPs. "\
     "• High morale and motivation. Expect a determined and persistent attack until either side has exhausted its combat effectiveness."\
     "• Freedom of movement across the surrounding terrain."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "UK"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{5080667C14A4F1A9}" {
     m_iOrder 4
     m_sTitle "Enemy forces"
     m_sContent "<h2>COMPOSITION & DISPOSITION</h2>  "\
     "Enemy forces consist of British Army infantry. Estimated strength is approximately 35 personnel, currently occupying their fortified platoon house, known locally as \"CIMIC House\", at GRID: 043039."\
     ""\
     "<h2>STRENGTHS & CAPABILITIES</h2>  "\
     "• A heavily fortified compound with multiple prepared fighting positions across several buildings, including machine gun emplacements. The compound is surrounded by a perimeter wall, which can be scaled."\
     "• Well-stocked with ammunition and supplies. Expect the British garrison to sustain a prolonged defence."\
     "• Almost all troops are issued optics."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_IRAQ"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{98A6755C51E23093}" {
     m_iOrder 5
     m_sTitle "Friendly forces"
     m_sContent "<h2>COMPOSITION & DISPOSITION</h2>  "\
     "We are 2nd Platoon, Y Company, 1st Battalion, Princess of Wales's Royal Regiment (1 PWRR).  "\
     "Our force consists of 30 personnel currently occupying our platoon house (CIMIC House) at GRID: 043039"\
     "We are restricted to our compound."\
     ""\
     "<h2>STRENGTHS & CAPABILITIES</h2> "\
     "• Three GPMG static machine guns have been set up around the compound within bunkers."\
     "• A large fortified compound enclosed by a perimeter wall, with the exception of a recent breach on the northeastern side. The compound contains multiple buildings, elevated fighting positions, and rooftop access, providing strong all-round defence."\
     "• Earth berms have been constructed along the inside of the perimeter wall, allowing personnel to fire over the wall while remaining behind cover."\
     "• one extra medic and one sniper are assigned to our garrison."\
     ""\
     "<h2>SERVICE & SUPPORT</h2>  "\
     "Our armoury and medical bay are both located on the ground floor of the main building. They contain additional ammunition, including a MAWs anti-tank launcher and LAW80s, as well as medical supplies, which should ideally be managed by the Platoon Sergeant."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "UK"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{6B380C609726674E}" {
     m_iOrder 6
     m_sTitle "Friendly forces"
     m_sContent "<h2>COMPOSITION & DISPOSITION</h2>  "\
     "We are Diina Company, otherwise known as the \"Mahdi Army\". "\
     "Our Squad is at the staging area and can choose to deploy at either the north, east, south, or west insert locations."\
     ""\
     "Our force consists of approximately 300 personnel operating throughout the area surrounding CIMIC House."\
     "The company is primarily composed of light infantry, supported by a limited number of motorised and armoured vehicles, including UAZs, BTRs, BRDMs, and BMPs."\
     ""\
     "The assault will be conducted in waves of approximately 60 personnel every five minutes from H-Hour."\
     ""\
     "<h2>STRENGTHS & CAPABILITIES</h2>  "\
     "• Freedom of movement throughout the area of operations. Other coalition forces are currently engaged elsewhere."\
     "• Significant superiority in manpower, allowing us to maintain continuous pressure through repeated assaults."\
     ""\
     "<h2>SERVICE & SUPPORT</h2>  "\
     "None. Resupply from captured equipment or what you carry."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_IRAQ"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{E40E5415628B4214}" {
     m_iOrder 7
     m_sTitle "Mission"
     m_sContent "<h2>MISSION STATEMENT</h2>  "\
     "Hold off the ongoing attack on our platoon house until the assaulting Iraqi forces withdraw."\
     ""\
     "<h2>MISSION DESCRIPTION</h2>  "\
     "Iraqi forces have launched a deliberate assault on our compound, opening the attack with an RPG strike that breached the northeastern perimeter wall. Their objective is to destroy the garrison and seize the platoon house, removing a key coalition foothold within the city."\
     ""\
     "Our position has become a significant obstacle to Iraqi operations, allowing us to monitor enemy activity and disrupt their freedom of movement throughout the area. As long as we hold the compound, they cannot operate freely within the city's area of operations."\
     ""\
     "Defend the compound, repel the assault, and deny the enemy control of this position until they are forced to break contact."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "UK"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{63AC5CDDAD89988A}" {
     m_iOrder 8
     m_sTitle "Mission"
     m_sContent "<h2>MISSION STATEMENT</h2>  "\
     "Conduct a DELIBERATE ASSAULT to OCCUPY the British platoon house and DESTROY the defending garrison."\
     ""\
     "<h2>MISSION DESCRIPTION</h2>  "\
     "British forces continue to occupy CIMIC House, using it as a fortified strongpoint to monitor our movements and disrupt operations throughout the area. As long as the compound remains in enemy hands, our freedom of movement and control of Al-Hadra will remain restricted."\
     ""\
     "The assault has already begun with an RPG strike breaching the northeastern perimeter wall. We must exploit the breach, overwhelm the defenders, and clear the compound before they can reorganise or receive support."\
     ""\
     "OCCUPY the compound, eliminate the British garrison, and restore our freedom of movement within the city."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_IRAQ"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{098FF5902B2158F5}" {
     m_iOrder 9
     m_sTitle "Comsig"
     m_sContent "<h2>CALLSIGNS</h2>"\
     "• HQ - 42"\
     "• OC - 42A"\
     "• PLT SGT - 42B"\
     "• 1 SEC - 42C"\
     "• 2 SEC - 42D"\
     "• 3 SEC- 42E"\
     ""\
     "<h2>FREQ/CHAN</h2>"\
     "• All callsigns - 42hz"\
     ""\
     "<h2>PASSWORDS</h2>"\
     "All can be changed at CO's discretion."\
     "• <b>Challenge:</b> Spectacle | <b>Password:</b> Paget"\
     "• Running password: 2"
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "UK"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{C296D2BDA0F3345D}" {
     m_iOrder 10
     m_sTitle "Mission notes"
     m_sContent "<h2>GM Notes</h2>"\
     "We rarely run COOP defence missions. This scenario is intended to test the server under sustained defensive gameplay, with players holding a fixed position against continuous enemy assaults."\
     ""\
     "If, at any point, the server is struggling or the assault feels too weak or too strong, GMs are encouraged to adjust enemy numbers and pacing accordingly."\
     ""\
     "• You are restricted to Iraqi 2000 infantry."\
     "• You may spawn <b>ONE</b> UAZ PKM, BTR, BRDM, and BMP each. A maximum of one vehicle type may be active at any one time.~"\
     "(No more than two vehicles at one time)"\
     ""\
     "<h2>End Conditions</h2>"\
     "<b>British Victory:</b>"\
     "• Hold off the Iraqi assault for 30 minutes."\
     ""\
     "<b>Iraqi Victory:</b>"\
     "• Overrun the British garrison by eliminating at least 85% (26/30) of British forces and occupy the compound."\
     ""\
     "<h2>Mission Notes</h2>"\
     "• E-tool usage is strictly forbidden and so is the use of any vehicle. These will break AI pathfinding in the compound. Leave everything as it is."\
     "• Iraqi forces only to be slotted if missions is <b>FULL</b> or if blufor accept the challenge."\
     "• JIP TP."\
     "• UK AO limit."\
     ""\
     "Mission made by TheLocalPub. Please use the <b>#feedback</b> channel on Discord to report issues or submit suggestions."
    }
    GC_Briefing "{FBFFC7B5A239321F}" {
     m_iOrder 11
     m_sTitle "Changelog"
     m_sContent "<h2>Changed:</h2>"\
     "• Adjust AI waypoint so they do less shooting and abit more moving now hopefully. Still trying to find the sweet spot."\
     "• Vehicles at spawn should hopefully not be accessible now. They were locked before, but I'm trying again."
    }
   }
  }
 }
}
